# tools/r/rota_grid_witness.rish -- the rota grid is an instruction to open twenty documents, and
# fifteen of them are written in a form no link wall reads.
#
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/r/rota_grid_witness.rish
#
# The 5 x 3 council grid in `recursion-prompts/seed/autonomous-loop.seed.md` is the one mechanism
# returning this tree's canon to living awareness on a schedule: each lap deep-reads one row -- the
# threshold page first, then its three seats. Measured at fleet scale `20260906.213125`, eight ships
# read the five rows 11, 12, 13, 20 and 12 times across 105 logs, so every document comes back
# roughly daily. That whole promise rests on twenty paths being right.
#
# NO GUARD WAS READING THOSE TWENTY PATHS AS A SET. The five thresholds are Markdown links; the
# fifteen seats are backticked bare paths, and `tools/fixtures/r/readme_reach_scan.sh` follows links
# alone. Fold a seat and the grid goes on naming a dead path in silence, while whatever OTHER citer
# linked that file reds instead -- so the repair lands over there and the grid stays wrong.
#
# THE DRIFT THAT ACTUALLY HAPPENED IS INVISIBLE TO EVERY LINK WALL BY CONSTRUCTION. Earth-Cardinal
# changed hands `20260905`, from `context/specs/20260627-102012_one-clock-naming-law.md` to
# `foundations/20260905-154954_the-clock-and-the-mark.md`, because a rota reads foundations and the
# mark law sat on no seat at all. The change reached the grid and not the Earth threshold page -- the
# FIRST thing an earth lap reads. **Both paths exist and both resolve.** Nothing was broken; the door
# opened on the seat it had replaced, which only a check comparing the door against the grid can see.
# A lap obeying the door got the clock half of the concern and missed the mark half, which was the
# whole reason the seat moved. Measured `20260907`: fourteen of fifteen seats agreed, and the one
# that did not was in the row being read that morning.
#
# A SEAT IS NAMED IN FOUR PLACES AND THIS GUARD READ THREE, found by the water rota `20260908.080219`.
# Every threshold page opens with a `**Kin:**` line naming its own three seats in modality order --
# the first line of the first page an element lap opens -- and BOTH seat changes this tree has ever
# made drifted there and nowhere else. Earth-Cardinal moved `20260905` and the Kin line kept the
# retired page BESIDE the new one, reading four seats where the grid seats three. Water-Cardinal
# moved `20260908` and the Kin line was never touched, so it named the released page and never named
# the live one -- while the grid, the heading, and the section path were all correct and this witness
# read GREEN. Widening it to the fourth site is what makes the door's own kin list a checked promise.

say "rota-grid: Language EN -- the twenty paths the canon's own schedule rests on."
say "rota-grid: Style Gauge, Meter -- four readings gated at zero, three reported."
say "rota-grid: Lens TAME -- bounds named at 5 rows and 3 seats, and every refusal shown from both sides."

say "rota-grid: the control -- twenty-five behaviors on a grid built for the purpose, in a pen..."
let ctl = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/r/rota_grid_control.sh"]
# invariant: both streams are written out BARE, ahead of the asserts that judge them. A bare `say`
# opens no `StrBuf`, so the report cannot refuse however large the output grows; an `else` clause
# interpolating the same value composes only on FAILURE, which is the one moment it is owed
# (`tools/s/say_compose_bound_witness.rish`).
say ctl.out
say ctl.err
assert ctl.ok else "rota-grid: the control refused -- its two streams stand above"
assert ctl.out contains "pass=25 fail=0" else "rota-grid: the control did not prove twenty-five behaviors -- its two streams stand above"

say "rota-grid: and the living grid answers..."
let scan = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/r/rota_grid_scan.sh"]
# invariant: a refusal reports BOTH streams. `run` returns `out` and `err` separately, and this
# scan writes every refusal to stderr -- so stdout alone leaves the roster's evidence page saying a
# guard stopped without saying why. Measured `20260907`: of 75 rostered witnesses that assert on a
# scan's `ok`, 14 report stdout alone and 3 report both. Both are said bare, once, and the seven
# asserts below then carry plain messages rather than seven copies of the same reading.
say scan.out
say scan.err
assert scan.ok else "rota-grid: the scan refused -- its two streams stand above"

# invariant: the shape is reported before any fault count, so a reader can tell a healthy grid from
# a grid the parser could not see. A scan that printed only faults would read zero on both.
assert scan.out contains "rows=5" else "rota-grid: the grid no longer parses five element rows"
assert scan.out contains "cells=15" else "rota-grid: the grid no longer parses fifteen cells"

# invariant: every path the grid names exists. A lap sent to a moved file reads nothing and its log
# records the row all the same, so absence here is silent by construction.
assert scan.out contains "unresolved=0" else "rota-grid: the grid names a document that is not on disk -- the reading stands above"

# invariant: every threshold page carries its three modality headings. The heading is the door a lap
# walks through first; without it there is nothing to check the seat against.
assert scan.out contains "sections_missing=0" else "rota-grid: a threshold page lost a modality section -- the reading stands above"

# invariant: each modality section names its own cell's seat. This is the drift that opened the row:
# a seat may change hands in the grid and leave the door pointing at the seat it replaced.
assert scan.out contains "seat_undeclared=0" else "rota-grid: a threshold page routes its reader to a seat the grid retired -- the reading stands above"

# invariant: each threshold's own `**Kin:**` line names all three of its live seats. This is the
# fourth site, and the only one both real seat changes drifted at -- compared by basename, since a
# Kin entry is relative to `foundations/` while the grid names a repo-root path.
assert scan.out contains "kin_seat_absent=0" else "rota-grid: a threshold's Kin line stopped naming a seat the grid gives it -- the reading stands above"

assert scan.out contains "verdict=ok" else "rota-grid: the grid reads drifted -- the reading stands above"

say "GREEN: rota-grid -- twenty paths named, twenty on disk, and every door and kin list opens onto the seat the grid seats."
